  "result": "The final gate verdict is **WITNESS_FAIL**, because of one witness: `branch_1` expects not applicable but gets violated. The other six witnesses pass (forbid, permit, idle, blind, branch_2, branch_3), and the gate raised no build, check, anchoring, claim, literal or vacuity problem. All 6 gate runs are used.\n\n**How the rule is written:**\n- **Green turn arrow alone:** the head shows a green left, right or U-turn arrow, and none of the other 20 signal states.\n- **Facing:** the distance test is |d|² ≤ reach², and the angle test is written without a square root as (h·d)·|h·d| ≥ cos·|cos|·|d|², which is exact for either sign of the cosine.\n- **The highway:** the head controls the intersection either directly or through a lane that enters it, and the intersection lies on the highway.\n- **Entering:** \"off the roadway at the previous observation\" is written with `rises`, since the language has no previous-observation operator. That makes the first instant of a trace unknown, so every witness sets its window to 1–3 s.\n- **Exceptions:** the four NRS 484B.283 exceptions are written as \"does not apply\" in the applicability, as the node specifies.\n- I added no narrowings.\n\n**Why `branch_1` fails:** the plan says NRS_484B_283_1d1 applies when the pedestrian head shows walk. I tried 9 walk scenes (and one where walk turns to flashing don't-walk). They changed:\n- where the pedestrian head stands;\n- what it governs: nothing, the roadway, the intersection, the lane, or combinations;\n- when walk comes on;\n- a marked crosswalk with its entrance recorded, and a far-side sidewalk;\n- the pedestrian's speed.\n\nIn every scene, all four composed rules came out decidedly not applying, not unknown. So something in their own conditions is false for this pedestrian. I'm not allowed to read those rules, so I can't tell what scene they need.\n\nOne more constraint matters here: the gate refuses a pedestrian signal that governs a crosswalk. The plan or repair session needs to check what NRS_484B_283_1d1 requires of a pedestrian at a walk signal. Then either describe that scene in `branch_1`, or repair 1d1 or re-plan `branch_1`. The rule and the other witnesses need no change.\n\nTwo process notes:\n- My first gate run had extra shell commands chained onto it. It still ran and counted as one of the 6.\n- After the last run I changed only a comment in the witness file's header (the pedestrian head's position and what it governs). It doesn't affect the build.\n\nThe full run log and the note for the plan agent are in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
